     POSIX threads are a set of functions that support applications with re‐
     quirements for multiple flows of control, called _t_h_r_e_a_d_s, within a
     process.  Multithreading is used to improve the performance of a program.

     The POSIX thread functions are summarized in this section in the follow‐
     ing groups:

           ••   Thread Routines
           ••   Attribute Object Routines
           ••   Mutex Routines
           ••   Condition Variable Routines
           ••   Read/Write Lock Routines
           ••   Per-Thread Context Routines
           ••   Cleanup Routines

     FreeBSD extensions to the POSIX thread functions are summarized in
     pthread_np(3).

